# text_id = 1608
# text = There was no finer cavalry material in the world than the English farmer , who provided his own horse , for they were accustomed to a certain amount of discipline in the hunting field , and the British farmer , officered by his neighbour , whom he often followed all over the country hunting , was the ideal cavalry solider .
