# text_id = 1633
# text = The construction of the canal was begun in the 18th century by a company incorporated in 1789 , and the cost was defrayed mainly by public subscriptions amounting to about £ 1,000,000 , and partly by Parliamentary grants amounting to some £ 360,000 , of which about £ 90,000 was granted by the Irish Parliament and the remainder after the Union .
