# text_id = 1735
# text = We ask the House to take on the Estimates 680,000 men , the Field Army absorbing 260,000 , the garrisons at home 190,000 , the Volunteers for London defence 100,000 , and the various staffs 4,000 , so that in all we have 560,000 men allotted to various positions , giving a margin of 120,000 for recruits not trained , the sick , and other deductions in time of war .
