# text_id = 1737
# text = The greater part of the agricultural land in this country is not worth anything like £ 100 an acre ; but , on the other hand , there is always the danger that if you put into an Act of Parliament a certain limit of value , the presumption — and it is not an unfair presumption — is that land over and above that value would not be agricultural land .
