# text_id = 1749
# text = Such language was never indulged in by a former Chief Secretary , the present First Lord of the Treasury , who had fought the Irish party vigorously , sometimes they thought unfairly , and had thrown hon . Members into prison as common felons because they were inspired by motives as worthy as his own ; but he had never sneered at the members of the Irish party for their poverty .
