# text_id = 1753
# text = The accountant of the Scottish Education Department went through the accounts of school boards , and called attention , where necessary , to what he regarded as illegal payments , but there was no power whatever of enforcing his opinion , however gross the malversation might have been ; and during the time he ( Lord Balfour ) was in office , cases arose where surcharges ought to have been made .
