# text_id = 1767
# text = Everybody agreed it was desirable that people should obtain sufficient knowledge to take a degree , and , whilst he admitted there were a great many arguments in favour of the association of persons in a University , he believed nothing but good could be said to have come from the system which at present existed in Ireland , and by which anybody could get a University degree if sufficiently clever .
