# text_id = 1771
# text = MR. SYDNEY BUXTON said there was no doubt some difficulty in finding a satisfactory form of words to limit the clerical element , but he thought the admission of the Parliamentary Secretary to the Board of Education that there might be cases of an undue preponderance of the clerical element on these bodies made it incumbent on the Government to provide that such an abuse as that should not occur .
