# text_id = 1783
# text = He thought the Bill repealed the hiring section of the Allotments Act of 1854 , but he was not sure that it repealed the purchase section , and , if those words were left in , he understood the point of his noble friend ( Lord Barnard ) was that the land might be acquired compulsorily under an Order made under some previous Act , and not under this Act .
