# text = The county councils were in that way in a position somewhat independent of the Local Government Board , and it was extremely undesirable that the officer whom they might have to consult with regard to the way they should use their discretion in enforcing some order on a defaulting authority should have his duties prescribed by a central authority in London who were unfamiliar with local conditions and circumstances .
