# text_id = 1828
# text = I know a great deal about these common lands in the Principality from which I come , and I think so far from the commoners objecting to any land being taken for afforestation , they would be very glad indeed to have it , on being compensated for their common rights , because afforestation does a great deal to cover and shelter the sheep now grazing on the Welsh hills .
