# text_id = 1832
# text = He understood his right hon . friend warned the House of Commons against forcing the hand of the Government , or compelling them to assume an attitude which might give rise to offence in foreign countries , but foreign countries did not consider British feeling ; they laid on every shilling of duty they could , and consistently framed their tariff arrangements according to their own necessities and requirements .
