# text = The Committee thought very strongly that it would be for the benefit of Ireland that the new route from the South of England by the Great Western Railway and the Fishguard and Rosslare Railway should be made as strong as possible , in order that there should be keen competition between the London and North Western Railway and the Great Western Railway for passengers and goods between England and Ireland .
