# text_id = 1835
# text = His own feeling was that in many cases the teacher did require some protection in this matter , and he ventured to think that a natural protection , to give , if it could be given anywhere in the Bill , was to say simply and in the plainest possible language that it should be the duty of all those who appoint teachers to have regard only to their obligatory duties .
