# text_id = 1857
# text = The noble Lord the Member for Woolwich , when he spoke of the War Office being rushed for guns , should not forget that , owing to the outbreak of the war , it became necessary to raise these fifteen batteries immediately , instead of gradually , and , in consequence , recourse had to be had to other manufacturers in order to supply the guns and thoroughly equip the batteries .
