# text_id = 1870
# text = MR . SMEATON ( Stirlingshire ) asked if these suspensions did not seriously retard the recovery of the peasants from the effects of famine , by compelling payment in the year immediately following the famine , and whether there was not evidence that this iron system of collection of revenue which should never be collected at all , had really been a contributory cause of the unrest in India ?
