# text_id = 1876
# text = His advices from South Africa , were to the effect that the Boers would not take any part in the government if that House decided to place upon them a form of representative government and that they would much prefer that the form of government should remain as it was than that what General Botha called a " bastard " form should be introduced before responsible government was granted .
