# text_id = 1889
# text = Following up this , I was looking up old files of The Times the other day and I saw that on the eve of Colenso Consols were rushing up because the City thought that Ladysmith was relieved , and the same thing happened — Consols were going up — on the night when our troops were pouring down the sides of Spion Kop and the Boers on the summit of it .
