# text_id = 1894
# text = To ask the President of the Board of Agriculture whether , in view of the outbreak of scab amongst the flocks of the United Kingdom , especially in England , he will consider the advisability of introducing a measure for the compulsory dipping of sheep for the prevention of scab , having regard to the fact that sheep scab has been prevented in New South Wales by such compulsory legislation .
