# text_id = 1915
# text = The great fault in judicial appointments in Ireland was , that they were made not from considerations of legal attainments , but from considerations of political services , and the hon . and learned Member and he would have been delighted if the Government upon this occasion had departed from the evil course followed by the Tory Government during the last ten years , and had appointed a political opponent .
